<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9729" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντέρως</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωτος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>return-love, love-for-love,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				255d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ach.Tat.
				1.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				24.305a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Anteros,</i> personified as <i>a god who avenged slighted
				love,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				1.30.1
			</span></i>, etc.:—but also (as it seems) <i>a god who
				struggled against</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔρως,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				6.23.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> name of a
				<i>gem,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				37.123
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
